{"id":"fm-fig-008","s":"further","t":"fp-de","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows the displacement of a particle moving with simple harmonic motion. Which equation of motion, with $x$ in metres and $t$ in seconds, fits the graph?","o":["$\\dfrac{d^2x}{dt^2}+\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}x=0$","$\\dfrac{d^2x}{dt^2}+\\pi^2x=0$","$\\dfrac{d^2x}{dt^2}+\\dfrac{\\pi^2}{4}x=0$","$\\dfrac{d^2x}{dt^2}+16x=0$"],"a":2,"x":"The graph repeats every 4 s (maximum at $t=0$, next at $t=4$), so $\\omega=2\\pi/4=\\pi/2$. SHM satisfies $\\ddot x+\\omega^2x=0$, so the equation is $\\ddot x+\\frac{\\pi^2}{4}x=0$.","w":["Found $\\omega=\\pi/2$ correctly but forgot that the equation needs $\\omega^2$, not $\\omega$.","Took the time from maximum to minimum (2 s) as the period, giving $\\omega=\\pi$ and $\\omega^2=\\pi^2$.","","Used the amplitude 4 on the graph, giving $\\omega^2=16$, instead of finding $\\omega$ from the period."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,8],"y":[-4,4],"xstep":1,"ystep":2,"xlabel":"time / s","ylabel":"displacement / m","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,4.0],[0.05,3.987669],[0.1,3.950753],[0.15,3.88948],[0.2,3.804226],[0.25,3.695518],[0.3,3.564026],[0.35,3.410561],[0.4,3.236068],[0.45,3.041624],[0.5,2.828427],[0.55,2.597792],[0.6,2.351141],[0.65,2.089994],[0.7,1.815962],[0.75,1.530734],[0.8,1.236068],[0.85,0.933781],[0.9,0.625738],[0.95,0.313836],[1.0,0.0],[1.05,-0.313836],[1.1,-0.625738],[1.15,-0.933781],[1.2,-1.236068],[1.25,-1.530734],[1.3,-1.815962],[1.35,-2.089994],[1.4,-2.351141],[1.45,-2.597792],[1.5,-2.828427],[1.55,-3.041624],[1.6,-3.236068],[1.65,-3.410561],[1.7,-3.564026],[1.75,-3.695518],[1.8,-3.804226],[1.85,-3.88948],[1.9,-3.950753],[1.95,-3.987669],[2.0,-4.0],[2.05,-3.987669],[2.1,-3.950753],[2.15,-3.88948],[2.2,-3.804226],[2.25,-3.695518],[2.3,-3.564026],[2.35,-3.410561],[2.4,-3.236068],[2.45,-3.041624],[2.5,-2.828427],[2.55,-2.597792],[2.6,-2.351141],[2.65,-2.089994],[2.7,-1.815962],[2.75,-1.530734],[2.8,-1.236068],[2.85,-0.933781],[2.9,-0.625738],[2.95,-0.313836],[3.0,-0.0],[3.05,0.31383