{"id":"fm-fig-009","s":"further","t":"fp-de","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows a damped oscillation $x=e^{-\\lambda t}(A\\cos\\omega t+B\\sin\\omega t)$ with $\\lambda>0$. The dashed curve is its envelope $x=Ce^{-\\lambda t}$ through P and Q. What is $\\lambda$?","o":["$\\frac{1}{2}\\ln 2$","$\\ln 2$","$\\frac{1}{2}$","$2\\ln 2$"],"a":0,"x":"The envelope passes through P at $t=0$ with $x=8$ and Q at $t=2$ with $x=4$. So $C=8$ and $8e^{-2\\lambda}=4$, giving $e^{-2\\lambda}=\\frac12$. Hence $2\\lambda=\\ln 2$ and $\\lambda=\\frac12\\ln2$.","w":["","Treated the amplitude as halving in 1 s, but the graph shows it halving between $t=0$ and $t=2$.","Used the 2 s interval and the halving to guess $\\lambda=\\frac12$, instead of solving $e^{-2\\lambda}=\\frac12$.","Solved $e^{-2\\lambda}=\\frac12$ as $\\lambda=2\\ln 2$, multiplying by the time instead of dividing."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,6],"y":[-8,8],"xstep":1,"ystep":2,"xlabel":"time / s","ylabel":"displacement / cm","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,8.0],[0.0375,7.841964],[0.075,7.579366],[0.1125,7.218525],[0.15,6.76696],[0.1875,6.233254],[0.225,5.626906],[0.2625,4.958178],[0.3,4.237934],[0.3375,3.477471],[0.375,2.688354],[0.4125,1.882249],[0.45,1.070756],[0.4875,0.265254],[0.525,-0.523254],[0.5625,-1.284284],[0.6,-2.007998],[0.6375,-2.685331],[0.675,-3.308091],[0.7125,-3.869052],[0.75,-4.362031],[0.7875,-4.781943],[0.825,-5.124847],[0.8625,-5.387969],[0.9,-5.569713],[0.9375,-5.669648],[0.975,-5.68849],[1.0125,-5.628058],[1.05,-5.491224],[1.0875,-5.281843],[1.125,-5.004676],[1.1625,-4.665302],[1.2,-4.270017],[1.2375,-3.825732],[1.275,-3.339856],[1.3125,-2.820188],[1.35,-2.274791],[1.3875,-1.71188],[1.425,-1.139702],[1.4625,-0.566419],[1.5,-0.0],[1.5375,0.551886],[1.575,1.081967],[1.6125,1.583462],[1.65,2.050156],[1.6875,2.47648],[1.725,2.857564],[1.7625,3.189291],[1.8,3.468332],[1.8375,3.692174],[1.875,3.859133],[1.9125,3.968356],[1.95,4.019811],[1.9875,4.014269],[2.025,3.953268],[2.0625,3.839076],[2.1,3.67464],[2.1375,3.463526],[